# Agent workflow

- Work in **large coherent phase deliveries**, not a chain of micro-approvals.
- Read the active phase document in `docs/development/phases/` before implementation.
- Do not advance to the next phase until the user explicitly approves/requests it.
- Do not ask about minor technical choices already resolvable by repository docs or standard engineering judgment.
- Ask only when a missing gameplay rule changes outcomes, requirements conflict materially, or scope would change.
- Before declaring a phase complete, run relevant tests, typecheck and build; fix failures introduced by your work.
- Update `PROJECT_STATUS.md` when a phase is ready for manual acceptance.
- End a phase with: implementation summary, run commands, automated checks, concrete manual test checklist, important decisions, real pending limitations.
- Keep documentation synchronized when making durable architectural decisions.
- Prefer useful implementation over ceremony. Do not spend disproportionate time adding low-value tests, abstractions or documents.
